infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Coordinating a multi-step process
  desc Choreography vs orchestration — pick by complexity and compensations
  compares
    - label Choreography
      children
        - label No central brain
          desc Each service listens for events and emits its own
        - label Logic = sum of reactions
          desc End-to-end flow lives nowhere — spread across services
        - label Maximally decoupled
          desc Great for simple, few-step flows
        - label No process state
          desc No one knows where order #8842 is, or who cleans up a stall
    - label Orchestration
      children
        - label Central coordinator / saga
          desc Explicitly drives the steps in order
        - label Flow in one readable place
          desc "Where is it?" has a single answer
        - label Compensating actions
          desc Refund, release stock to unwind on failure
        - label Reintroduces a knower
          desc One component knows everyone — best for complex, must-not-half-complete flows
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
